"Jew":{"w":"Jew","firstLevel":"初中","cn":"n. 犹太人； 犹太教徒","senses":[{"pos":"n","cn":["犹太人","犹太教徒"]}],"ph":{"uk":"/dʒuː/","ukSrc":"有道","us":"/dʒuː/","usSrc":"有道"},"audio":{"url":"https://dict.youdao.com/dictvoice?audio=Jew&type=2","src":"有道真人发音"},"ex":[{"en":"Mr Sarkozy, whose maternal grandfather was a <B>Jew</B> from Salonika, is the first French president born after the war.","cn":"萨科齐是第一位战后出生的法国总统，其外祖父是来自萨洛尼卡的犹太人。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"A more fanciful theory is that Mr. Sarkozy has a natural sympathy for the country that was home to his maternal grandfather, a <B>Jew</B> from Thessaloniki.","cn":"一个更稀奇的推测说，萨科奇先生对于其外祖父的祖国有一种天然的同情，他的外祖父是来自塞萨洛尼基的犹太人。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"And you would call yourself an Orthodox <B>Jew</B>. -yes.","cn":"你称自己是犹太教正统派，-是的。","src":"有道例句","srcType":"dict","srcFull":"有道词典双语例句（接口未标注具体词典）"},{"en":"Imagine if a Catholic, a Protestant, a <B>Jew</B>, tried to get away with that.","cn":"","src":"FORBES","srcType":"news","srcFull":"新闻语料 · FORBES"}],"fam":{"root":"","affix":[],"derive":[{"w":"jewish","ph":"","cn":"adj. 犹太人的"}],"syn":[]},"tag":[],"collins":0,"oxford":0,"frq":0,"img":"","syl":{"n":1,"s":0,"l":["Jew"]},"flags":["no_exam_ex","no_img","fam_gap"]},
